P1.7: validate ingest-derived argv; SSRF-guard the AI endpoint

Asset metadata (compose file_path, systemd unit name, volume name, mountpoint,
image ref) becomes a subprocess argv token, and under federation those fields
can arrive from a secondary's /ingest payload. Validate before execve:
- _reject_optlike(): refuse a leading-dash value (parsed as an option flag) or
  one carrying NUL/CR/LF. Applied to unit name, volume name, mountpoint, image ref.
- _validate_compose_file(): a compose -f target must be absolute, carry a
  recognized compose basename, have no traversal, and resolve under a configured
  discovery root (projects_root/direct_roots/scan_roots).

ai.py: gate the operator-configurable AI endpoint. Block cloud instance-metadata
hosts (169.254.169.254 etc.) outright so a mis/maliciously-set endpoint can't
turn the server into an SSRF proxy; optional INFRADOCS_AI_ALLOWED_HOSTS locks it
to an explicit allow-list. Local Ollama/vLLM on localhost/LAN still works.

